        "id": 214611,
        "name": "cnranger",
        "username": "cnranger",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/53a042/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-02-16T17:44:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>It was interesting to hear how thier approach to Kickstarter games has changed from:</p><p>Are people interested in a thing? They are! Let's make it. or They aren't! Let's not make it.</p><p>to:</p><p>Are people interested in this thing we are already working on (30%, 50%, 70% done)? They are! We will finish it. or They aren't! Scrap all that work.</p><p>The turnaround for successful projects would be quicker with the second method but the risk of wasted work for failed projects is higher too.</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
